# Go backend conventions

- Put business logic in `pkg/services/<domain>/`, not in API handlers.
- Keep service interfaces in the same package as their implementations.
- Use `sqlstore` for database access and gRPC/protobuf for plugin communication.
- Use the applicable `oss`, `enterprise`, or `pro` build tag.
- Check for a directory-scoped `AGENTS.md` before changing a specialized subtree.

## Dependency injection and verification

- After changing service initialization or Wire dependencies, run `make gen-go`.
- Prefer a targeted test first: `go test -run TestName ./path/to/package/`.
- Use `make test-go-unit` for the full unit suite and `make lint-go` for Go linting when warranted.
- Backend packages such as `pkg/api/` can take minutes to compile, so keep test scope proportional to the change.
